# Architecture

- Respect existing boundaries: UI, domain, data, infrastructure, and integration layers should not silently collapse into one another.
- Prefer composition and dependency injection over hidden global state.
- Keep business rules deterministic and testable where practical.
- Add an abstraction only when it removes real coupling or repeated complexity; avoid speculative frameworks.
- For APIs and schemas, preserve backward compatibility unless a breaking change is explicitly intended.
- Make failure modes explicit at integration boundaries.
- When changing architecture, document the why, migration path, and rollback story.
